WEBVTT

NOTE tts=synthetic

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
When should a breaker bushing be replaced?

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.400
As a bushing wears, the clearance between tool and bushing grows.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.400
Measure between the tool shank and the bushing bore; past the limit, replace the bushing.

4
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:22.800
Too much side play of the tool, an oval bore and wear on one side of the tool shank show a worn bushing.

5
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:29.800
Check the front and the thrust bushing together; make sure the bushing seat in the front head is sound.
